 "interpretation": {
  "synthesis": "7. Synthesis: the 6-9-month rebound was not observed in lung LCNEC (RR 0.97 (0.84-1.11)). Across the 2 x 2 layout the point estimates are consistent with the rebound being associated with small-cell morphology, but the evidence rests mainly on the lung small- vs large-cell contrast (1.43 (1.24-1.64)). The colorectal subtype contrast is imprecise (1.48 (0.89-2.46)), and an organ effect comparable to the morphology effect is not excluded (colorectal/lung 1.27 (0.93-1.73) for small-cell; 1.22 (0.80-1.88) for large-cell). The interaction estimate (1.04 (0.61-1.76)) is too imprecise to show that the morphology effect is the same in both organs.",
